    </TIER>
    <TIER LINGUISTIC_TYPE_REF="translation" PARENT_REF="transcription" TIER_ID="translation">
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a66" ANNOTATION_REF="a1">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Do you know about munmaanta'qw?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a67" ANNOTATION_REF="a2">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yes, I know about that...
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a68" ANNOTATION_REF="a3">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's what you can speak about.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a69" ANNOTATION_REF="a4">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>When a new baby boy is born, it is never…
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a70" ANNOTATION_REF="a5">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Her uncles seemed to be evil people.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a71" ANNOTATION_REF="a6">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>There was just one person that was doing that, but maybe there were more.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a72" ANNOTATION_REF="a7">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>As soon as the baby was born, the uncle would go to see if it was a girl.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a73" ANNOTATION_REF="a8">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If it was a girl, they would just leave the baby alone.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a74" ANNOTATION_REF="a9">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>If it was a boy, they would kill it.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a75" ANNOTATION_REF="a10">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>None of the boys were left alive to grow.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a76" ANNOTATION_REF="a11">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then, one day, another girl had a baby, and she hid the baby boy's thing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a77" ANNOTATION_REF="a12">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when the uncle got there, he felt the baby to make sure it was really a girl, and then he left it alone and went away.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a78" ANNOTATION_REF="a13">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they heard the baby when it cried.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a79" ANNOTATION_REF="a14">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[And then the uncle said,] “That baby that's crying really sounds like a boy.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a80" ANNOTATION_REF="a15">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>You'd better go examine it again.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a81" ANNOTATION_REF="a16">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So again, they went to do that, and they arrived there.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a82" ANNOTATION_REF="a17">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, they asked again if it was really a girl.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a83" ANNOTATION_REF="a18">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“It's really a girl, a girl”, the mother said.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a84" ANNOTATION_REF="a19">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Eventually, she decided to flee.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a85" ANNOTATION_REF="a20">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Very early in the morning, she left, walking.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a86" ANNOTATION_REF="a21">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Was it the chief that was doing all that?
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a87" ANNOTATION_REF="a22">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Aha, he was a warrior.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a88" ANNOTATION_REF="a23">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He did those bad things for whatever reason.Maybe he was uneasy about [losing his status,] whatever...
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a89" ANNOTATION_REF="a24">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he killed them, like how the First People used to kill each other.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a90" ANNOTATION_REF="a25">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so that woman fled, walking upstream.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a91" ANNOTATION_REF="a26">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>She kept walking until she arrived to shxuxeey'elu.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a92" ANNOTATION_REF="a27">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the baby was crying, and that's where she bathed him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a93" ANNOTATION_REF="a28">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>After she finished bathing the child, then she started walking again until she reached Quamichan.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a94" ANNOTATION_REF="a29">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then she bathed him again, and she had a shell, whatever kind of shell—horse clam or whatever.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a95" ANNOTATION_REF="a30">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They were different then,  </ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a96" ANNOTATION_REF="a31">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>She laid him down and prepared [a bath], put water in a container, and she bathed her baby.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a97" ANNOTATION_REF="a32">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's why it's referred to as Little Dish, that place on your land.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a158" ANNOTATION_REF="a98">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's a little dish.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a159" ANNOTATION_REF="a99">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>After all that she did, she started to walk again, and she came uphill towards Amelia Bob's place, getting to where the church was.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a160" ANNOTATION_REF="a100">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What's the name of that place?


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a161" ANNOTATION_REF="a101">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Reaching that place, her baby was crying non-stop again.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a162" ANNOTATION_REF="a102">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And she bathed him again, using that shell.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a163" ANNOTATION_REF="a103">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And again, she filled it with water, and again she bathed her child.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a164" ANNOTATION_REF="a104">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>After she finished doing that, she started walking again.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a165" ANNOTATION_REF="a105">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And thus, they named that place ts'e'wi'tun.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a166" ANNOTATION_REF="a106">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's why they are calling that place ts'e'wi'tun.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a167" ANNOTATION_REF="a107">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>St. Peters, Dish. 	&lt;PN&gt;
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a168" ANNOTATION_REF="a108">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yes, and the one at your land is the little dish, the small one, and its name means small.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a169" ANNOTATION_REF="a109">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then again, she started to walk.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a170" ANNOTATION_REF="a110">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then she started to follow the creek, here to hwkw'sutsum.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a171" ANNOTATION_REF="a111">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then she got as far as a place over there.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a172" ANNOTATION_REF="a112">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And indeed, there was a big rock in that place where she was, and they camped out there, building their home.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a173" ANNOTATION_REF="a113">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Where they lived was a good place for catching trout for them to eat.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a174" ANNOTATION_REF="a114">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then... no, I jumped in my story and got ahead in what I said.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a175" ANNOTATION_REF="a115">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I got too far ahead.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a176" ANNOTATION_REF="a116">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He kept bathing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a177" ANNOTATION_REF="a117">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He was bathing... I'll keep going...
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a178" ANNOTATION_REF="a118">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He kept bathing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a179" ANNOTATION_REF="a119">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He scrubbed himself, scrubbed with the boughs.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a180" ANNOTATION_REF="a120">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when he was doing that, he would shake the boughs.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a181" ANNOTATION_REF="a121">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And when they hit in the water, they started to swim...
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a182" ANNOTATION_REF="a122">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The nettles from the boughs started to swim.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a183" ANNOTATION_REF="a123">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They hit the water, and what was swimming turned into trout.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a184" ANNOTATION_REF="a124">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Every time he bathed, that happened.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a185" ANNOTATION_REF="a125">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He shook the branch, and the nettles hit the water and would start swimming.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a186" ANNOTATION_REF="a126">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>They would turn into trout, little trout, fingerlings.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a187" ANNOTATION_REF="a127">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, this is where the trout came from.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a188" ANNOTATION_REF="a128">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It's because of Q'ise'q taking a bath that the trout appeared.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a195" ANNOTATION_REF="a189">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He's telling this story clearly; good.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a196" ANNOTATION_REF="a190">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's why the trout is here at Quamichan.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a197" ANNOTATION_REF="a191">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And perhaps that's why that place is known as Hwkw'sutsum, 'place full of trout'.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a272" ANNOTATION_REF="a198">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That big boulder is there, and that's Q'ise'q's mother.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a273" ANNOTATION_REF="a199">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And that's where he was growing.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a274" ANNOTATION_REF="a200">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then the mother warned him, “Don't go too far that way, son.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a275" ANNOTATION_REF="a201">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Just stay close by when you play.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a276" ANNOTATION_REF="a202">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He was holding a bow and arrow that was prepared for him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a277" ANNOTATION_REF="a203">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he started hunting the birds, fixing them, pulling the skins off the birds, and they were sewn together to make an outfit.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a278" ANNOTATION_REF="a204">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>All the different species of birds that he killed were in his outfit.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a279" ANNOTATION_REF="a205">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he arrived at that place where he was bathed.



</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a280" ANNOTATION_REF="a206">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was getting strong and becoming a young man.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a281" ANNOTATION_REF="a207">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He lay down on the bluffs, where it was beautiful, just lying there, reclining.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a391" ANNOTATION_REF="a208">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>At hwkw'ukw'uqe'num'.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a392" ANNOTATION_REF="a209">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And something came flying by, and it saw the beautiful outfit that he had on, warming himself on the bluff.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a393" ANNOTATION_REF="a210">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he came flying down, circling around him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a394" ANNOTATION_REF="a211">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He circled around him again, and then he came down and landed near him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a395" ANNOTATION_REF="a212">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he went close to the one that was lying on his back, and spoke to him, “Your outfit is very beautiful.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a396" ANNOTATION_REF="a213">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I'm really wanting your outfit.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a397" ANNOTATION_REF="a214">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I want to take your outfit, and you can exchange it for my outfit.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a398" ANNOTATION_REF="a215">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And if you agree and put it on, you will be able to fly, 
the way I was flying before I landed.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a399" ANNOTATION_REF="a216">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he says “I really want my outfit.”</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a400" ANNOTATION_REF="a217">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“But I'm really wanting your outfit.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a401" ANNOTATION_REF="a218">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Well, perhaps if you really want it, I will give it to you and...”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a402" ANNOTATION_REF="a219">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Ah, okay! And if you use this, you can try to fly; go and do it now.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a403" ANNOTATION_REF="a220">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, he put it on; Q'ise'q did put it on.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a404" ANNOTATION_REF="a221">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so, he told him, “Try to do it like this, then.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a405" ANNOTATION_REF="a222">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he did this, and he started to tremble.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a406" ANNOTATION_REF="a223">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he started to fly, Q'ise'q did.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a407" ANNOTATION_REF="a224">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he was told that he had done enough and to go back and return.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a444" ANNOTATION_REF="a225">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Oh, you're good! You did good.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a445" ANNOTATION_REF="a226">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>You did it just the way I told you.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a446" ANNOTATION_REF="a227">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Okay, you can have my outfit then.”


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a447" ANNOTATION_REF="a228">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>"good"</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a448" ANNOTATION_REF="a229">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>So, they traded, and the one that was flying wore Q'ise'q's outfit, and he ended up just walking.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a449" ANNOTATION_REF="a230">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And Q'ise'q was able to fly.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a450" ANNOTATION_REF="a231">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And Q'ise'q just flew off, and he went to where his mother was.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a451" ANNOTATION_REF="a232">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he went flying, circling around his mother.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a452" ANNOTATION_REF="a233">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What he was wearing made a loud flapping sound.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a453" ANNOTATION_REF="a234">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The noise of his outfit was quite loud.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a454" ANNOTATION_REF="a235">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And then he would just hide his outfit.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a455" ANNOTATION_REF="a236">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he would just walk home to his mother.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a456" ANNOTATION_REF="a237">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>He arrived and she told him, “Son, whatever was that, I wonder, that was that was flying around?
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a457" ANNOTATION_REF="a238">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It came around here, and I got really scared.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a458" ANNOTATION_REF="a239">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he pretended that he didn't know what it was, even though it was actually him.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a459" ANNOTATION_REF="a240">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Then he started thinking that he wanted to go to the place that his mother forbade him ever to go to.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a460" ANNOTATION_REF="a241">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>“Okay, I'm going to go take a look.”
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a461" ANNOTATION_REF="a242">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And so, on the next day, he went off.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a626" ANNOTATION_REF="a243">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he arrived there.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a627" ANNOTATION_REF="a244">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he didn't really show himself; he just landed.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a628" ANNOTATION_REF="a245">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And he saw the ones playing a ball game called qi'qtum'as, either qi'qtum'as or, what is is called, ts'uqwula'.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a629" ANNOTATION_REF="a246">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think what they were playing was called ts'uqwula'.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a630" ANNOTATION_REF="a247">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>A deer's tail was attached to it, and they were throwing it.


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a631" ANNOTATION_REF="a248">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And they were catching it just like a baseball.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a632" ANNOTATION_REF="a249">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The tail was attached to it, and it would be thrown to their own team.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a633" ANNOTATION_REF="a282">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the one that catches it would run.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a634" ANNOTATION_REF="a283">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>The knot of a tree was what they made their ball from.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a635" ANNOTATION_REF="a284">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>It was from the vine maple tree.
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a636" ANNOTATION_REF="a285">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think it was the vine maple tree that you find that kind of [knot].


</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a637" ANNOTATION_REF="a286">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the deer tail was attached to it...
</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a638" ANNOTATION_REF="a287">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And the deer tail was attached to it.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </REF_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <REF_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a639" ANNOTATION_REF="a288">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>And that's how... what is it called... the thing they were throwing was identified.
